# Use-case 01 gap 1 (claim C4, corrected): a type() whose ARGUMENT is a
# conjunction containing a reference — the `type($.std.Service & {...})`
# vocabulary idiom — breaks every use site.  On the current engine the
# use site is SILENTLY DROPPED from generation (exit 0, `use` missing),
# in one file just as under @"..." include; the README's loud
# [aontu/mapval_no_gen] was not reproducible for this shape.  --canon
# shows `use` fully unified and concrete, so this is silent data loss.
# Controls that generate `use` correctly: type() removed; or the
# reference moved to a FIELD of the type body (`Entry: type({base:
# $.Base, owner: string})`); spec row edge.tsv:edge-type-template pins
# the no-inner-reference case as generating.
# expected: {"Base":{"kind":"service"},
#            "use":{"kind":"service","owner":"team-pay"}} exit 0
# actual:   {"Base":{"kind":"service"}} exit 0 — `use` silently gone
Base: { kind: "service" }
Entry: type($.Base & { owner: string })
use: $.Entry & { owner: "team-pay" }
